        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-2 text-lightblue">From Spectator to Steward: Your Guide to Hands-On Conservation</h2>
        <p class="text-white/80">Bali's underwater realm is a global treasure, a vibrant metropolis of biodiversity within the Coral Triangle. As divers, we are privileged witnesses to its beauty, but we also see its fragility. This guide is for the diver who wants to do more than just observe. It’s a practical roadmap to transform your passion for the ocean into tangible action, moving from spectator to an active steward of the reefs.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
        <p>It’s no secret: Bali lies at the epicentre of the Coral Triangle, boasting the planet's highest marine biodiversity. But this ecological masterpiece faces immense pressure from climate change, plastic pollution, and coastal development. The good news? The diving community is stepping up. Conservation diving in Bali isn’t just a niche activity; it's a growing movement. It offers a profoundly rewarding way to give back, ensuring the reefs you love today can thrive for generations to come.</p>

        <br class="my-3">
        <h3 class="text-gold">Your Mission Brief: Key Conservation Focus Areas</h3>
        <ul class="list-none pl-0 space-y-3 my-4">
